## API Reference

### `useEffect`

The `useEffect` hook is used to run and cleanup the effect after unmounting, with an optional callback that will be executed after the component is unmounted.

```jsx
import { useEffect } from 'react'

export default function Page() {
  useEffect(() => {
    // Run your cleanup function when the component unmounts
    return () => {
      // Cleanup logic
    }
  }, [])

  // ... rest of your page
}
```

### `useEffectEvent`

The `useEffectEvent` hook allows you to listen to an event. This is useful when you need to trigger an action after a component unmounts.

```jsx
import { useEffectEvent } from 'react'

export default function Page() {
  const handleClick = useEffectEvent(() => {
    // Run your cleanup function when the component unmounts
    return () => {
      // Cleanup logic
    }
  })

  return (
    <button onClick={handleClick}>
      Click me
    </button>
  )
}
```

### `useLayoutEffect`

The `useLayoutEffect` hook allows you to run layout effects. This is useful when you need to apply a layout to the document's body.

